sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Admin as Merchant Admin (Browser)
    participant Civi as Customer CiviCRM (Self-Hosted PHP Backend)
    participant OAuth as SumUp OAuth Server
    participant API as SumUp REST API

    Note over Civi: Installation-specific client ID and client secret are configured locally
    Note over Civi: OAuth tokens are stored locally per CiviCRM payment processor

    Admin->>Civi: Click "Connect to SumUp"
    Note over Civi: Generate a random state value<br/>Store state, processor ID and exact redirect URI<br/>in the CiviCRM cache for 10 minutes

    Civi-->>Admin: 302 Location: https://api.sumup.com/authorize
    Admin->>OAuth: GET /authorize<br/>response_type=code<br/>client_id=CLIENT_ID<br/>redirect_uri=EXACT_CALLBACK_URL<br/>scope=REQUESTED_SCOPES<br/>state=STATE
    Note over OAuth: REQUESTED_SCOPES = payments payment_instruments<br/>transactions.history readers.read readers.write<br/>user.profile_readonly

    Admin->>OAuth: Authenticate and grant permissions
    OAuth-->>Admin: 302 Location: EXACT_CALLBACK_URL?code=AUTH_CODE&state=STATE
    Admin->>Civi: GET EXACT_CALLBACK_URL?code=AUTH_CODE&state=STATE

    Note over Civi: Read and delete the cached state<br/>Reject a missing, reused or expired state
    Civi->>OAuth: POST https://api.sumup.com/token<br/>Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded<br/>grant_type=authorization_code<br/>code=AUTH_CODE<br/>client_id=CLIENT_ID<br/>client_secret=CLIENT_SECRET<br/>redirect_uri=EXACT_CALLBACK_URL
    OAuth-->>Civi: 200 access_token, refresh_token,<br/>expires_in and granted scope

    Civi->>API: Resolve the authorised merchant identity<br/>Authorization: Bearer ACCESS_TOKEN
    API-->>Civi: Merchant profile or memberships

    Note over Civi: Require exactly one merchant code<br/>Store tokens, granted scope, expiry and merchant code locally
    Civi-->>Admin: 302 Redirect to the local SumUp connection page
    Note over Admin,Civi: Display "SumUp merchant MERCHANT_CODE is now connected"

    opt A SumUp API call needs a token that expires within 60 seconds
        Civi->>Civi: Acquire the payment-processor-scoped refresh lock
        Civi->>OAuth: POST https://api.sumup.com/token<br/>Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded<br/>grant_type=refresh_token<br/>refresh_token=REFRESH_TOKEN<br/>client_id=CLIENT_ID<br/>client_secret=CLIENT_SECRET
        OAuth-->>Civi: 200 new access_token,<br/>expires_in and optional new refresh_token
        Note over Civi: Update the local token record<br/>Keep the previous refresh token if none is returned
    end
